{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>These are the commandments and the ordinances.</b> The third book, which is the book of Leviticus, called תורת כהנים, is sealed with the verse ״אלה המצות אשר צוה ה׳ את משה״ — 'These are the commandments which YHWH commanded Moses,' and this fourth book is likewise sealed with the verse אלה המצות. It added והמשפטים ('and the ordinances') because it mentioned the ordinances of inheritance and the ordinances of the murderers." "<b>And you should consider</b> why there it mentioned 'with Moses' (את משה) but did not mention 'by the hand of Moses' (ביד משה), whereas here it mentioned 'by the hand of Moses' (ביד משה). The matter is that the first covenant, which was at Horeb — they received it, until at the King's banquet they nullified it, and exchanged their glory for the likeness of an ox that feeds on grass (תבנית שור המירוהו), and it became the destroyer of their majesty; they did not succeed in it and it did not endure in their hands. And the faithful messenger, upon seeing the letters flying, cast the tablets from his hands. But here, in the plains of Moab, in the second covenant, the covenant between HaShem and them was established — though mountains may depart and every rock be displaced from its place, this covenant shall not be annulled, and the bond of love shall not be severed. Through the tradition of His covenant He brought us to fame and praise, and we took upon ourselves the words of the covenant under oath — ״ואלה״ ('and these'); and from this you will find at the end of the Torah a verse that pairs with it: <b>״אלה דברי הברית אשר כרת ה׳ את משה לכרות את בני ישראל בארץ מואב מלבד הברית אשר כרת אתם בחורב״.</b> <br><b>The book of Numbers is concluded.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:07.683641372Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}